        "property": {
          "$bytes": "e3e363d1dd294ccb8e6ff3b76d99bc33"
        },
        "value": {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "## Cohorts and study design\n\nBirth cohorts: 1972–1976. The source describes 120 initial families and a study sample of 114 subjects (58 treatment and 56 control). These recruitment and study counts differ from outcome-specific analysis samples. School-age support involved a separate randomization.\n\n## Relationship to the economic analysis\n\nThe economic paper pools first-phase ABC and CARE center-based treatment against their randomized controls. It does not constitute a third independent trial. Control children could attend alternative formal childcare, and life-cycle forecasts extend beyond observed follow-up.\n\n[Source: 2. ABC/CARE: Background](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7331936/)",
          "language": {
            "$bytes": "090adac0fca4822e8e719263e67620ec"
          }
        }
      }
    ],
    "unset": []
  },
