        "value": {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "## Cohorts and study design\n\nBirth cohorts: 1978–1980. The source describes 65 initial families: 17 assigned to center-based childcare, 25 to family education and 23 to control. The life-cycle economic analysis excludes the home-visiting-only family-education arm.\n\n## Relationship to the economic analysis\n\nThe economic paper pools first-phase ABC and CARE center-based treatment against their randomized controls. It does not constitute a third independent trial. Control children could attend alternative formal childcare, and life-cycle forecasts extend beyond observed follow-up.\n\n[Source: 2. ABC/CARE: Background](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7331936/)",
          "language": {
            "$bytes": "090adac0fca4822e8e719263e67620ec"
